senses.gloss:
प्र-तापन, अस्, ई, अम्, making hot, paining,
distressing, tormenting; (अस्), m. a particular hell;
(अम्), n. warming, heating; burning, consuming;
inflicting pain or punishment, paining, distressing.

प्र-तरम्, ind., Ved. further; more, more espe-
cially, more exceedingly; principally, pre-eminently;
(Sāy. = प्रकृष्टतरम्, अतिशयेन.)

प्रातर प्रातर, अस्, m., N. of a Nāga; (in
Gaṇa Kṛśāsvādi to Pāṇ. IV. 2, 80, a various reading
for प्रतर.)
